WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Open a saved scenario. Its name, notes, tracts,
and assumptions return from PostgreSQL.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Change assumed adoption from 30% to 35%.
The calculator updates immediately. These are fictional inputs.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Save creates revision 2.
The original revision remains available.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Select revision 1 for export.
Later edits do not change this saved snapshot.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The conflict review shows this tab's 45% draft
beside the latest saved value of 36%. Nothing is overwritten.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Duplicate the retained draft and name a new scenario
for the retry demonstration.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The service is stopped. The save fails with a useful message.
The draft and retry key stay on the page.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Restart the service and retry the same request.
It saves once as revision 1, with the original draft intact.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Refresh the page and reopen the saved scenario.
The account, notes, tract selection, and assumptions survive.
